1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,720
Busan can feel like a lot of city to

2
00:00:02,720 --> 00:00:04,480
cover in one day.

3
00:00:04,480 --> 00:00:07,080
The coast stretches a long way

4
00:00:07,080 --> 00:00:09,440
so the trick is not to race from one

5
00:00:09,440 --> 00:00:10,960
side to the other.

6
00:00:10,960 --> 00:00:13,260
Stay on the east coast for a temple above

7
00:00:13,260 --> 00:00:14,340
the sea

8
00:00:14,340 --> 00:00:16,020
a relaxed beach stop

9
00:00:16,020 --> 00:00:17,220
a Korean spa

10
00:00:17,220 --> 00:00:19,260
and dinner near the water.

11
00:00:19,260 --> 00:00:21,540
Here is a simple route that keeps the day

12
00:00:21,540 --> 00:00:23,940
moving without turning it into a marathon.

13
00:00:24,498 --> 00:00:26,338
This is the order:

14
00:00:26,338 --> 00:00:28,198
start at Haedong Yonggungsa

15
00:00:28,198 --> 00:00:31,058
return to Haeundae for the beach and lunch

16
00:00:31,058 --> 00:00:33,878
spend the afternoon at SPA LAND in Centum City

17
00:00:33,878 --> 00:00:36,398
then come back to Haeundae for dinner.

18
00:00:36,398 --> 00:00:38,618
The map shows the four main stops.

19
00:00:39,348 --> 00:00:42,788
One day on Busan’s east coast.

20
00:00:42,788 --> 00:00:45,268
Let’s make the most of it without trying to

21
00:00:45,268 --> 00:00:46,988
see the whole city at once.

22
00:00:47,358 --> 00:00:49,938
Coming from Seoul is possible

23
00:00:49,938 --> 00:00:51,998
but it makes for a long day.

24
00:00:51,998 --> 00:00:54,898
The KTX from Seoul Station to Busan Station

25
00:00:54,898 --> 00:00:57,738
takes about two and a half hours.

26
00:00:57,738 --> 00:00:59,658
Busan Station is on the other side of the

27
00:00:59,658 --> 00:01:01,218
city from Haeundae

28
00:01:01,218 --> 00:01:03,798
so the trip across town adds time.

29
00:01:03,798 --> 00:01:05,318
If this is your plan

30
00:01:05,318 --> 00:01:07,458
think about staying at least one night rather

31
00:01:07,458 --> 00:01:09,438
than trying to squeeze everything into a

32
00:01:09,438 --> 00:01:10,258
return day.

33
00:01:10,656 --> 00:01:12,976
For this itinerary

34
00:01:12,976 --> 00:01:15,796
staying near Haeundae the night before makes

35
00:01:15,796 --> 00:01:17,776
the morning simpler.

36
00:01:17,776 --> 00:01:20,836
Haedong Yonggungsa is north-east of Haeundae

37
00:01:20,836 --> 00:01:24,176
and the first ride is the longest transfer in

38
00:01:24,176 --> 00:01:25,656
this plan.

39
00:01:25,656 --> 00:01:28,136
You can also stay near the temple in the

40
00:01:28,136 --> 00:01:29,356
Osiria area

41
00:01:29,356 --> 00:01:31,696
but that makes more sense if you want to

42
00:01:31,696 --> 00:01:33,956
wake up there or have plans nearby.

43
00:01:34,410 --> 00:01:37,950
Bring the same transit card you use in Seoul.

44
00:01:37,950 --> 00:01:40,810
It works on Busan’s subway and buses.

45
00:01:40,810 --> 00:01:41,630
For directions

46
00:01:41,630 --> 00:01:42,970
use Naver Map or KakaoMap

47
00:01:42,970 --> 00:01:45,830
especially for the current local bus route to

48
00:01:45,830 --> 00:01:46,470
the temple.

49
00:01:46,470 --> 00:01:49,350
Taxis are the easiest way to reach Haedong

50
00:01:49,350 --> 00:01:50,890
Yonggungsa from Haeundae.

51
00:01:50,890 --> 00:01:53,630
You can show the driver the name on your

52
00:01:53,630 --> 00:01:53,990
map app

53
00:01:53,990 --> 00:01:56,290
or book with the Kakao T app.

54
00:01:56,676 --> 00:01:59,553
Check opening hours on a map app on the day

55
00:01:59,553 --> 00:02:02,065
especially for SPA LAND and the Haeundae

56
00:02:02,065 --> 00:02:02,954
Blueline Park.

57
00:02:02,954 --> 00:02:05,360
If you want to ride the sky capsules

58
00:02:05,360 --> 00:02:08,133
book ahead in summer and on weekends because

59
00:02:08,133 --> 00:02:09,493
tickets can sell out.

60
00:02:09,493 --> 00:02:12,109
Summer weekends at Haeundae are busy, too

61
00:02:12,109 --> 00:02:14,882
so start early and save the beach for later

62
00:02:14,882 --> 00:02:16,176
in the morning.

63
00:02:16,782 --> 00:02:21,002
The route follows the coast in a sensible order.

64
00:02:21,002 --> 00:02:22,422
Go north-east first

65
00:02:22,422 --> 00:02:26,202
then come back toward Haeundae and Centum City.

66
00:02:26,202 --> 00:02:28,822
You will still need to travel between stops

67
00:02:28,822 --> 00:02:31,362
but you avoid spending the day crossing back

68
00:02:31,362 --> 00:02:33,062
and forth across Busan.

69
00:02:33,696 --> 00:02:35,900
Start early at Haedong Yonggungsa

70
00:02:35,900 --> 00:02:38,984
a Buddhist temple built on rocks above the sea

71
00:02:38,984 --> 00:02:39,701
in Gijang.

72
00:02:39,701 --> 00:02:42,400
Most Korean temples sit in the mountains

73
00:02:42,400 --> 00:02:45,320
so this shoreline setting is what makes this

74
00:02:45,320 --> 00:02:46,311
one stand out.

75
00:02:46,311 --> 00:02:48,294
It gets busy from mid-morning

76
00:02:48,294 --> 00:02:50,828
which is another reason to begin here.

77
00:02:50,828 --> 00:02:51,765
From Haeundae

78
00:02:51,765 --> 00:02:54,684
a taxi takes around twenty to thirty minutes

79
00:02:54,684 --> 00:02:56,062
depending on traffic.

80
00:02:56,062 --> 00:02:57,494
Local buses also run

81
00:02:57,494 --> 00:03:00,524
so check the current route before setting off.

82
00:03:00,524 --> 00:03:02,892
Allow about an hour for your visit.

83
00:03:02,892 --> 00:03:05,482
There are steps down to the main hall.

84
00:03:05,482 --> 00:03:07,355
This is a place of worship

85
00:03:07,355 --> 00:03:10,440
so keep your voice low and be considerate when

86
00:03:10,440 --> 00:03:11,676
taking photos.

87
00:03:12,498 --> 00:03:13,585
After the temple

88
00:03:13,585 --> 00:03:15,345
head back to Haeundae Beach.

89
00:03:15,345 --> 00:03:17,365
Keep this part of the day easy:

90
00:03:17,365 --> 00:03:19,746
walk along the sand and the promenade

91
00:03:19,746 --> 00:03:22,749
then find lunch in the streets behind the beach.

92
00:03:22,749 --> 00:03:25,389
Haeundae Traditional Market is a short walk

93
00:03:25,389 --> 00:03:27,822
from the sand and is a handy place to

94
00:03:27,822 --> 00:03:30,929
look for snacks such as fish cakes and tteokbokki.

95
00:03:30,929 --> 00:03:33,880
If you have time and want another coastal ride

96
00:03:33,880 --> 00:03:36,675
the Haeundae Blueline Park runs a beach train

97
00:03:36,675 --> 00:03:39,937
and small sky capsules along the old coastal railway

98
00:03:39,937 --> 00:03:43,302
between Mipo near the end of the beach and Cheongsapo.

99
00:03:43,302 --> 00:03:44,907
Check the current details

100
00:03:44,907 --> 00:03:48,158
and book sky capsules ahead during busy periods.

101
00:03:48,756 --> 00:03:50,876
In the afternoon

102
00:03:50,876 --> 00:03:53,256
take the subway one stop from Haeundae to

103
00:03:53,256 --> 00:03:55,676
Centum City on Line Two.

104
00:03:55,676 --> 00:03:58,416
SPA LAND is inside Shinsegae Centum City

105
00:03:58,416 --> 00:03:59,576
department store.

106
00:03:59,576 --> 00:04:03,616
It has hot-spring baths and themed rest rooms

107
00:04:03,616 --> 00:04:05,676
making it a comfortable introduction to Korean

108
00:04:05,676 --> 00:04:07,496
bathhouse culture.

109
00:04:07,496 --> 00:04:10,116
Give yourself time to slow down here instead

110
00:04:10,116 --> 00:04:11,816
of treating it as a quick photo stop.

111
00:04:11,816 --> 00:04:15,396
The department store is in the same building

112
00:04:15,396 --> 00:04:17,756
so it is also a useful indoor option if

113
00:04:17,756 --> 00:04:19,636
the weather turns.

114
00:04:19,636 --> 00:04:22,036
Check SPA LAND’s hours before you go.

115
00:04:22,470 --> 00:04:23,530
For dinner

116
00:04:23,530 --> 00:04:25,450
return to Haeundae.

117
00:04:25,450 --> 00:04:27,670
Ribs of Legend Haeundae is close to the beach

118
00:04:27,670 --> 00:04:30,630
and serves Korean grilled ribs.

119
00:04:30,630 --> 00:04:31,230
After eating

120
00:04:31,230 --> 00:04:32,990
you can take a gentle walk along the beach

121
00:04:32,990 --> 00:04:34,250
at night.

122
00:04:34,250 --> 00:04:36,750
If you would rather see another stretch of coast

123
00:04:36,750 --> 00:04:39,430
take a short taxi ride to Gwangalli Beach

124
00:04:39,430 --> 00:04:42,310
where Gwangan Bridge is lit up after dark.

125
00:04:42,310 --> 00:04:44,070
Choose one easy finish;

126
00:04:44,070 --> 00:04:46,890
you do not need to add another long cross-city trip.

127
00:04:47,736 --> 00:04:50,236
The day is easiest if you think of it

128
00:04:50,236 --> 00:04:54,156
as one longer ride followed by short local trips.

129
00:04:54,156 --> 00:04:56,036
Use a taxi or a checked bus route for

130
00:04:56,036 --> 00:04:56,956
the temple.

131
00:04:56,956 --> 00:04:58,636
Then return to Haeundae

132
00:04:58,636 --> 00:05:00,856
where the beach and market are close together

133
00:05:00,856 --> 00:05:02,016
on foot.

134
00:05:02,016 --> 00:05:03,236
For Centum City

135
00:05:03,236 --> 00:05:06,096
take Line Two one stop from Haeundae.

136
00:05:06,096 --> 00:05:07,256
After the spa

137
00:05:07,256 --> 00:05:09,516
return to Haeundae for dinner.

138
00:05:09,516 --> 00:05:11,676
Traffic can affect the taxi ride to the temple

139
00:05:11,676 --> 00:05:14,296
so leave room in your plan rather than relying

140
00:05:14,296 --> 00:05:16,216
on an exact arrival time.

141
00:05:16,842 --> 00:05:19,402
A few choices can make this day harder than

142
00:05:19,402 --> 00:05:20,862
it needs to be.

143
00:05:20,862 --> 00:05:22,762
Avoid these common planning mistakes.

144
00:05:24,204 --> 00:05:24,631
First

145
00:05:24,631 --> 00:05:27,456
do not leave the temple until the middle of

146
00:05:27,456 --> 00:05:28,043
the day;

147
00:05:28,043 --> 00:05:29,962
it gets busy from mid-morning

148
00:05:29,962 --> 00:05:31,561
so an early start helps.

149
00:05:31,561 --> 00:05:32,041
Second

150
00:05:32,041 --> 00:05:34,813
remember that Busan Station is on the other

151
00:05:34,813 --> 00:05:36,839
side of the city from Haeundae.

152
00:05:36,839 --> 00:05:39,185
The subway trip takes about an hour

153
00:05:39,185 --> 00:05:41,904
so build that into a day trip from Seoul.

154
00:05:41,904 --> 00:05:42,330
Third

155
00:05:42,330 --> 00:05:45,636
resist adding the west side of Busan to this route.

156
00:05:45,636 --> 00:05:46,969
Jagalchi Fish Market

157
00:05:46,969 --> 00:05:47,768
BIFF Square

158
00:05:47,768 --> 00:05:50,594
and Gamcheon Culture Village are better saved

159
00:05:50,594 --> 00:05:51,767
for a second day.

160
00:05:51,767 --> 00:05:52,300
Finally

161
00:05:52,300 --> 00:05:54,859
check opening hours and current transport

162
00:05:54,859 --> 00:05:56,138
details on the day

163
00:05:56,138 --> 00:05:59,424
particularly for the spa and the Blueline Park.

164
00:05:59,910 --> 00:06:03,310
Can you visit Busan as a day trip from Seoul?

165
00:06:03,310 --> 00:06:04,070
Yes

166
00:06:04,070 --> 00:06:06,170
the KTX makes it possible

167
00:06:06,170 --> 00:06:08,170
but it will be a long day.

168
00:06:08,170 --> 00:06:09,830
You will see more if you stay at least

169
00:06:09,830 --> 00:06:11,370
one night

170
00:06:11,370 --> 00:06:13,410
ideally near Haeundae for this plan.

171
00:06:13,968 --> 00:06:17,527
What is the simplest way to reach Haedong Yonggungsa?

172
00:06:17,527 --> 00:06:19,335
Take a taxi from Haeundae.

173
00:06:19,335 --> 00:06:22,329
The ride is around twenty to thirty minutes

174
00:06:22,329 --> 00:06:23,741
depending on traffic.

175
00:06:23,741 --> 00:06:25,549
Local buses also go there

176
00:06:25,549 --> 00:06:29,408
so check the current route in Naver Map or KakaoMap.

177
00:06:30,018 --> 00:06:33,278
Does this plan work on a rainy day?

178
00:06:33,278 --> 00:06:34,058
Partly.

179
00:06:34,058 --> 00:06:36,258
The temple and beach are outdoors

180
00:06:36,258 --> 00:06:40,458
but SPA LAND and Shinsegae Centum City are indoors.

181
00:06:40,458 --> 00:06:42,118
If the weather is poor

182
00:06:42,118 --> 00:06:44,458
you can give the afternoon more time and keep

183
00:06:44,458 --> 00:06:46,358
the outdoor stops flexible.

184
00:06:46,884 --> 00:06:49,564
Here is the day in one line:

185
00:06:49,564 --> 00:06:52,324
start early at Haedong Yonggungsa

186
00:06:52,324 --> 00:06:55,524
spend late morning and lunch around Haeundae Beach

187
00:06:55,524 --> 00:06:57,484
rest at SPA LAND in Centum City

188
00:06:57,484 --> 00:07:00,144
then return to Haeundae for dinner.

189
00:07:00,144 --> 00:07:01,624
Use your transit card

190
00:07:01,624 --> 00:07:03,264
check current hours and routes

191
00:07:03,264 --> 00:07:06,004
and keep your plans on the east side of Busan.

192
00:07:06,004 --> 00:07:07,244
The full guide

193
00:07:07,244 --> 00:07:08,924
with links for every stop

194
00:07:08,924 --> 00:07:10,464
is on Korea Plainly.

195
00:07:10,464 --> 00:07:12,484
The link is in the description.

196
00:07:12,484 --> 00:07:13,644
If this helped

197
00:07:13,644 --> 00:07:15,464
subscribe for more plain

198
00:07:15,464 --> 00:07:16,604
practical guides to Korea.

